<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Klosterneuburg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Klosterneuburg is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> just north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>. It was briefly a residence of the Babenberg margraves, and Leopold III founded its Augustinian abbey in 1114, which became the burial place of the saint and holds the enamelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a> Altar of Nicholas of Verdun (1181). The abbey is one of the richest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/klosterneuburg.jpg" alt="Klosterneuburg" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C.Stadler/Bwag · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Klosterneuburg_(1).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
